# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
~$*

# Local dependency / build output (for the future production app).
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not style.
# `node_modules/` on its own matches a directory at ANY depth, and Metro's web
# export writes a package's own assets under their real path. So the four Outfit
# font files landed in `assets/node_modules/@expo-google-fonts/outfit/...` and
# git refused all four on every publish, without a word. The live site served
# four 404s and rendered the whole app in the phone's system font for weeks.
# Bupe reported it twice as "the fonts are not correct" before it was found.
#
# An anchored pattern only ever means the real dependency directory at the repo
# root, which is the only thing that was ever meant. tools/check-deploy.mjs is
# the second line: it fails a publish that references a file git will not carry.
/node_modules/
/dist/
/build/
/.expo/

# Python bytecode from the tools/ scripts (reground.py and friends)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
